          "url": "https://x.com/badlogicgames/status/2116078693827428383",
          "topic": "Durable agent execution with database commits and crash recovery",
          "text": "people of pi (durable). i did a round of performance optimizations in pi-durable.\n\nquick primer. every step of an agent run is saved to a db before the agent moves on. 1 save = 1 commit. thats what makes it durable, crash mid run, resume from the last commit. ~12 commits per run",
